  \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-43\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-44\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"searched\": [\n    \"no repository: this is new build work\"\n   ],\n   \"span\": \"I-45\"\n  }\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"assumptions\": [\n  \"Later or answered assumptions win: ASM-30 'Price on request' (also for deactivated price lists) over ASM-2; ASM-31 (prices excluding tax, invoices add tax at one configurable rate) over ASM-3; ASM-35 (one persistent basket per Buyer) over ASM-13; Q-8 (block quantities above last imported quantity at submission and confirmation, no subtraction of orders since import) over ASM-7.\",\n  \"Order emails go to the Buyer who placed the order; for staff-created orders they go to the customer company's contact email (ASM-39).\",\n  \"Every staff cancellation, not only rejection, requires a reason that is emailed to the customer (ASM-40).\",\n  \"Stock CSV rows are matched on the unique distributor product code; a product never included in a successful import counts as Out of stock (ASM-41).\",\n  \"A stock file is invalid as a whole if missing, unreadable, lacking the identifier or quantity column, or containing any quantity that is not a whole number ≥ 0; unknown identifiers alone do not invalidate it.\",\n  \"Product images: JPEG, PNG or WebP up to 5 MB; a new upload replaces the previous image (ASM-42).\",\n  \"Reports use net amounts of invoices dated in the selected range, so cancelled and undelivered orders are excluded; 'top products' means the top 20 (ASM-44).\",\n  \"Repeating an order adds to the existing basket, summing quantities for products already present (ASM-45).\",\n  \"Invoice tax is calculated on the net total and rounded to 2 decimals half-up (ASM-46).\",\n  \"An order must keep at least one line; removing every line is done by cancellation. Order notes are limited to 1000 characters.\",\n  \"Price validation at submission rejects if any price changed since review and returns the new prices for confirmation.\",\n  \"Office Staff can view but not edit customer pricing; only Administrators manage catalogue, price lists, users and settings.\",\n  \"d1 AC-17.2 wording was garbled; the merged AC-21.2 uses the consistent reading (Friday 15:00 with that week's Tuesday as a holiday gives the following Tuesday).\",\n  \"Test class names in drafts (StockStatusPolicy/Resolver, DeliveryDateCalculator, InvoiceStatusPolicy/Resolver) are proposals only; no code exists yet.\",\n  \"NFR numbers are proposed targets since the request gives none; where drafts differed the majority or stricter value was used.\"\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n   \"metric\": \"p95 ≤ 1.0 s with 50,000 active products and 50 concurrent users\",\n   \"text\": \"Catalogue text, category and vehicle searches respond within the target with 50 concurrent users (d3 proposes a 100,000-product catalogue; d2 proposes p95 ≤ 1.5 s).\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n   \"metric\": \"p95 ≤ 2.0 s at 50 concurrent users\",\n   \"text\": \"Order submission (including stock and price validation for baskets up to 100 lines), basket, order list and order detail calls respond within the target.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n   \"metric\": \"≤ 15 minutes end to end\",\n   \"text\": \"The nightly stock import finishes within the target for a 100,000-row file (d2 proposes ≤ 10 minutes).\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n   \"metric\": \"p95 ≤ 5 s\",\n   \"text\": \"Invoice PDF generation completes within the target for invoices up to 200 lines (d2 proposes ≤ 3 s).\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n   \"metric\": \"bcrypt cost ≥ 12 or Argon2id (≥ 64 MB memory); 0 plaintext passwords in database and log scan\",\n   \"text\": \"Passwords are stored only as salted adaptive hashes; no plaintext or reversibly encrypted password appears in storage or logs.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n   \"metric\": \"100% of endpoints over TLS 1.2 or higher; plain HTTP redirected (301)\",\n   \"text\": \"All traffic is served over encrypted transport.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n   \"metric\": \"Idle timeout 30 minutes; absolute session lifetime 12 hours\",\n   \"text\": \"Sessions expire after inactivity (reading of d1 and d3).\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n   \"metric\": \"Session invalid after 8 hours of inactivity\",\n   \"text\": \"Sessions expire after inactivity (reading of d2; conflicts with NFR-7).\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-9\",\n   \"metric\": \"≥ 99.5% monthly\",\n   \"text\": \"Portal availability during business hours (07:00–19:00 configured timezone, working days), hosted in one cloud region.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-10\",\n   \"metric\": \"≥ 7 years retention; 0 deletions\",\n   \"text\": \"Audit entries, orders and invoices are retained and never deleted by any application function or user deactivation.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-11\",\n   \"metric\": \"WCAG 2.1 AA, 0 critical failures in automated audit\",\n   \"text\": \"Customer-facing screens (sign-in, catalogue, product, basket, checkout, orders, invoices) meet accessibility standards.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"NFR-12\",\n   \"metric\": \"≥ 99% handed off within 60 s\",\n   \"text\": \"Order and status emails are handed to the email service promptly after the triggering action (d2 proposes 2 minutes, d3 5 minutes).\"\n  }\n ],\n \"outOfScope\": [\n  \"Customer Account Manager role; all Buyers see all company orders and invoices (Q-1)\",\n  \"Customer-created or customer-edited delivery addresses (Q-5)\",\n  \"Templates shared across Buyers of a company (Q-6)\",\n  \"Backorders and ordering quantities above the last imported stock quantity (Q-8)\",\n  \"Writing stock to the ERP or decrementing/reserving stock in the portal between imports (Q-8)\",\n  \"Online card payments and payment method capture\",\n  \"Route planning for deliveries\",\n  \"SMS or push notifications; editable email templates (ASM-15, ASM-25, ASM-26)\",\n  \"Social login or single sign-on (ASM-36)\",\n  \"Nested categories (ASM-19, ASM-37)\",\n  \"Multiple currencies (ASM-4)\",\n  \"Volume, promotional, discount and effective-dated pricing\",\n  \"Migration of existing customers, products, price lists and users; system starts empty with seed data (ASM-23)\",\n  \"Custom report builder (ASM-21)\",\n  \"Bulk import of vehicle compatibility data; entered manually by admins (ASM-20)\",\n  \"Separate Rejected order status (ASM-14, ASM-38)\",\n  \"Reproducing an existing client invoice template\",\n  \"Multi-region hosting; one cloud region in the client's account (ASM-24)\"\n ],\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An active Customer Buyer of company A with password 'Correct#1'\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Response is 200 with a session; GET /me with that session returns role 'Customer Buyer' and company A, and GET /orders returns 200\",\n     \"when\": \"POST /auth/sign-in with that email and 'Correct#1'\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An active account buyer@a.test\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Both return 401 with the same message 'Invalid email or password' and no session is issued\",\n     \"when\": \"Sign-in is called with buyer@a.test and a wrong password, and separately with unregistered unknown@a.test\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a user submits an email address and password that match an active account, the portal shall start an authenticated session that carries the user's role and, for a Customer Buyer, the user's customer company.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"ASM-36\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A signed-in user\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Sign-out returns 200 and the later request returns 401\",\n     \"when\": \"POST /auth/sign-out, then a request is made with the same session token\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a signed-in user signs out, the portal shall invalidate that user's session.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An active account with 4 consecutive failed attempts\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Both responses give the 'account temporarily locked' message and no session is issued\",\n     \"when\": \"A 5th wrong password is submitted, then the correct password 1 minute later\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An account locked at 10:00\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Sign-in is rejected with the lock message\",\n     \"when\": \"The correct password is submitted at 10:14\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An account locked at 10:00\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Sign-in succeeds and the failed-attempt counter is reset to 0\",\n     \"when\": \"The correct password is submitted at 10:15:01\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An account with 4 consecutive failed attempts\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-3.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The account is not locked\",\n     \"when\": \"A successful sign-in occurs, followed by 4 more failed attempts\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If 5 consecutive sign-in attempts for one account fail, then the portal shall lock that account for 15 minutes and reject every sign-in attempt for it during that time with a message saying the account is temporarily locked.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"ASM-5\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A registered user and an unregistered email address\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Both responses are identical; one reset email is sent for the registered user and none for the unregistered address\",\n     \"when\": \"POST /auth/password-reset is called for each\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A reset link issued 30 minutes ago\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The new password signs in, the old one returns 401, and the second use of the link is rejected\",\n     \"when\": \"The user sets a new password through it, signs in with old and new passwords, then uses the link again\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A reset link issued at 09:00\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The reset is rejected as expired and the password is unchanged\",\n     \"when\": \"It is used at 10:00:01\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An account locked by failed attempts at 10:00\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-4.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Sign-in is still rejected as locked until 10:15\",\n     \"when\": \"The user resets the password at 10:05 and signs in with the new password at 10:06\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When a user requests a password reset for their email address, the portal shall email that address a single-use reset link that is valid for 1 hour and lets the user set a new password.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"ASM-16\",\n    \"ASM-17\",\n    \"ASM-36\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An admin invites new@a.test as Customer Buyer of company A\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The account becomes Active and the invitee can sign in\",\n     \"when\": \"The invitee uses the emailed link 2 days later to set a password\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An invitation sent 7 days and 1 minute ago\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The request is rejected as expired and the account stays Invited\",\n     \"when\": \"The invitee uses the link\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An expired or pending invitation\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"A new link valid for 7 days is emailed and the previous link is rejected\",\n     \"when\": \"The admin resends it\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An admin\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-5.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The request is rejected with 400 because the role does not exist\",\n     \"when\": \"The admin invites a user with role 'Customer Account Manager'\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator invites a Customer Buyer for a customer company or an Office Staff user, the portal shall email the invitee a link, valid for 7 days, through which the invitee sets a password and the account becomes active.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-17\",\n    \"ASM-16\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A deactivated Buyer with 3 past orders\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Sign-in is rejected with an 'account inactive' message and staff can still open all 3 orders unchanged\",\n     \"when\": \"The Buyer signs in with the correct password\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Buyer with an open session whose company is then set inactive, and the company has a Received order\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Response is 403, no order is created and the existing order stays Received\",\n     \"when\": \"The Buyer submits a checkout\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Buyer with an open session who is then deactivated\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Response is 403 and no order is created\",\n     \"when\": \"The Buyer submits a checkout\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A deactivated user\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-6.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Sign-in succeeds\",\n     \"when\": \"An admin reactivates the user and the user signs in\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"If a user has been deactivated or the user's customer company is inactive, then the portal shall reject that user's sign-in and order submissions while keeping the user's and company's existing orders, invoices and history unchanged.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-17\",\n    \"ASM-18\",\n    \"ASM-34\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Users in roles Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator with statuses Invited, Active and Deactivated\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Each user is returned with role, company (Buyers only) and status\",\n     \"when\": \"An admin lists users\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A signed-in Buyer with past orders\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The user's next request returns 401, sign-in is rejected, and past orders remain visible to staff\",\n     \"when\": \"The admin deactivates the user\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A Buyer of company A\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Only company B's orders are returned\",\n     \"when\": \"An admin moves the Buyer to company B and the Buyer lists orders\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An active Office Staff user S\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Response is 400 and S keeps the Office Staff role\",\n     \"when\": \"An admin changes S's role to Customer Buyer without a company\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An Office Staff user\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-7.5\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Response is 403\",\n     \"when\": \"The user calls PATCH /admin/users/{id}\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"When an administrator lists users, deactivates or reactivates a user, changes a user's role between Customer Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator, or changes a Customer Buyer's company, the portal shall show each user's role, company and account status, keep every Customer Buyer linked to exactly one customer company, apply the change from the user's next request, and keep the user's historical records.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-17\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Buyer X of company A, and an order, invoice and invoice PDF of company B\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Each returns 404 and no company B data is returned\",\n     \"when\": \"Buyer X requests each by ID\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Company A with orders placed by Buyer X, Buyer Y and Office Staff\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"All 3 orders are returned and no other company's orders\",\n     \"when\": \"Buyer X lists orders\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Buyer X of company A\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"Response is 404\",\n     \"when\": \"Buyer X requests company B's delivery addresses or account details by ID\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An unauthenticated client\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-8.4\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"All return 401\",\n     \"when\": \"It calls the catalogue, order or invoice endpoints\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The portal shall restrict each Customer Buyer to the orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account details of the Buyer's own customer company.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-8\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-9\",\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-1\",\n    \"Q-2\"\n   